# ============================================================================
# PLACEHOLDER: Place your small-molecule SDF file here (optional)
# ============================================================================
#
# If your simulation includes a docked or crystal small molecule (a ligand
# or substrate), place its SDF file in this directory.
#
# SMALL-MOLECULE SDF FILE (optional):
#   - 3D coordinates (from docking, a crystal structure, or conformer
#     generation), in the frame of the protein PDB
#   - Hydrogens and formal charges for your simulation pH
#   - One conformer is simplest; with several, pick one with
#     `conformer_index` (0 = first)
#   - Name it as the `sdf_path` of a `type: small_molecule` entry under
#     `solutes:` in config.yaml, for example:
#
#       solutes:
#         - type: small_molecule
#           name: "substrate"
#           sdf_path: "structures/ligand_Y.sdf"
#           conformer_index: 0
#
#   The file must be SDF (.sdf). Other formats are not read.
#
# ATOM NAMES: an SDF usually has no atom names, so in the built system each
# atom of the small molecule is named by its element, its count among the
# atoms of that element in the SDF's order, and an "x" suffix (C1x, C2x,
# H1x, ...). Use these names in restraint selections; `polyzymd validate`
# lists them when a selection names an atom the molecule will not have.
#
# If you are not simulating a small molecule, delete this placeholder and
# leave the `type: small_molecule` entry in config.yaml commented out.
# ============================================================================
